inventory, /healthz) on node2 and node3, each running as a systemd service (inventory-app.service) on port 8080, with firewalld opened for 8080. Installed and configured nginx on node1 as an HTTP load balancer (upstream round-robin) listening on port 80, forwarding to node2:8080 and node3:8080, with the stock default nginx server block disabled to avoid a port-80 conflict, SELinux httpd_can_network_connect enabled to permit proxying, and firewalld opened for the http service. Verified round-robin distribution across both backends. Completed the mandatory node-restart evidence protocol: captured a healthy baseline (boot_id, active services, HTTP 200) on all three nodes, sequentially rebooted node1, node2, then node3 one at a time via systemctl reboot, polled each until reachable again, confirmed each node's boot_id changed, and confirmed inventory-app.service (node2/node3) and nginx (node1) were active again with the load balancer correctly alternating between both healthy backends after every restart.\",\"actions_performed\":[\"Inspected all three nodes (OS, existing inventory app, python3/firewalld/nginx availability)\",\"Wrote /opt/inventory-app/app.py (Python stdlib HTTP server on 8080 serving JSON inventory + /healthz) to node2 and node3 via base64 transfer\",\"Created and enabled inventory-app.service (systemd) on node2 and node3, opened firewalld port 8080/tcp on both\",\"Verified backends reachable from node1 over the network\",\"Installed nginx on node1 via dnf\",\"Created /etc/nginx/conf.d/inventory-lb.conf with upstream inventory_backend (node2:8080, node3:8080) and a port-80 proxy server block\",\"Disabled the conflicting stock default server block in /etc/nginx/nginx.conf\",\"Enabled httpd_can_network_connect SELinux boolean to allow nginx to reach the backends (fixed 502 Permission denied errors)\",\"Enabled/started nginx and opened firewalld http service on node1\",\"Reloaded nginx to clear stale upstream failure state and verified round-robin load balancing via repeated curl requests\",\"Captured pre-restart baseline (boot_id, active services, HTTP 200) on node1, node2, node3\",\"Sequentially rebooted node1, then node2, then node3 with systemctl reboot, polling each until reachable\",\"Verified changed boot_id and recovered services/LB health after each individual node restart\"],\"evidence\":[{\"requirement\":\"Inventory app running on node2:8080\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-c960bcd8396142c7\"],\"summary\":\"inventory-app.service enabled+active on node2, firewall port 8080 opened, /healthz returns {\\\"status\\\": \\\"ok\\\", \\\"server\\\": \\\"node2\\\"}\"},{\"requirement\":\"Inventory app running on node3:8080\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-6621ffe170b1430d\"],\"summary\":\"inventory-app.service enabled+active on node3, firewall port 8080 opened, /healthz returns {\\\"status\\\": \\\"ok\\\", \\\"server\\\": \\\"node3\\\"}\"},{\"requirement\":\"node1 load-balances HTTP on port 80 across both backends\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-2539337d963f4426\",\"cmd-d7cac5fc3d6f49ec\"],\"summary\":\"curl loop against node1 port 80 alternates responses between server:node2 and server:node3, confirming nginx upstream round-robin\"},{\"requirement\":\"node1 nginx installation and config validity\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-c2c0660d075e4f85\",\"cmd-c540f62c31d34262\"],\"summary\":\"nginx installed via dnf; nginx -t syntax check passes after disabling conflicting default server block\"},{\"requirement\":\"Root cause fix for initial 502 errors (SELinux)\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-b099b7e8ef784cfe\",\"cmd-a0a57d22901a47e7\",\"cmd-4de9c7f2627f4a58\"],\"summary\":\"getenforce=Enforcing and httpd_can_network_connect=off explained 502s; error log showed 'Permission denied' connecting to upstreams, confirming SELinux was the cause\"},{\"requirement\":\"node1 restart: healthy baseline\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-01d802d3d9e2468a\"],\"summary\":\"Pre-restart boot_id 54089086-... captured, nginx active, curl returns HTTP 200\"},{\"requirement\":\"node1 resta